  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual material as the speaker of the joke",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material (text_chunk_1 and text_chunk_2) because the meme presents a first-person narrative ('she said... so I told her...'), inviting the viewer to identify with the speaker who is making the misogynistic statement. The user is not explicitly deictic (e.g., 'me' or 'you'), but the framing of the joke as a personal retort creates an implicit projection of the user as the one who 'told her' to get back in the kitchen, thereby aligning the user with the speaker of the misogynistic sentiment.",
